-- title:
--   Degree of level N₀ℓ q over level N₀ q
-- statement:
--   For a natural number $N_0 \neq 0$ and primes $q, \ell$ with $\ell \neq q$, write $F_M \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull M`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field `LaurentSeries ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of all $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ j_q$ for nonzero divisors $d \mid M$. Let $\varphi \colon F_{N_0 q} \to F_{N_0 \ell q}$ be a ring homomorphism which is compatible with the two inclusions into `LaurentSeries ℚ`, i.e. for every $f \in F_{N_0 q}$ the Laurent series underlying $\varphi(f)$ equals the Laurent series underlying $f$. Then, with respect to the $F_{N_0 q}$-module structure on $F_{N_0 \ell q}$ induced by $\varphi$, the rank `Module.finrank` of $F_{N_0 \ell q}$ over $F_{N_0 q}$ equals $\ell$ if $\ell \mid N_0$, and $\ell + 1$ otherwise. Note that the hypothesis on $\varphi$ forces it to be the inclusion of $F_{N_0 q}$ into $F_{N_0 \ell q}$ read through the ambient Laurent series field, so the assertion is a statement about the degree of that field extension.
--
--   Classically this is the index $[\Gamma_0(N_0 q) : \Gamma_0(N_0 \ell q)] = \psi(N_0 \ell q)/\psi(N_0 q)$, the degree of the covering $X_0(N_0 \ell q) \to X_0(N_0 q)$ expressed on function fields. It is used in the computation of the degree of the degeneracy maps entering [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isFinite_flat_finrank_curveChange_heckeDegeneracy_rat`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isFinite_flat_finrank_curveChange_heckeDegeneracy_rat).
